# ACT ONE

= A windbound evening. Two oldfriendsandalampthatwon'tstaylit.

# SCENE 1

A single oil lamp on awooden table,centrestage.ELENAsitsbeside it, reading.The lightflickers.Outside,awindthathas been blowingfor three days issomehowloudernow.

ELENA
(without looking up)
You're back early.

MARCUS enters from the wings, brushing snow from his coat.

MARCUS
The road's closed past the bridge.
ELENA
Then sit down before you melt on the carpet.

MARCUS sits opposite her. The lampgutters.Bothlookatit,thenat each other.

ELENA
Don't.
MARCUS
I haven't done anything.
ELENA
You were about to.

A long pause. The windeasesforamoment,andinthegapMARCUSspeaks more quietlythanhemeansto.

MARCUS
I had a letter today.
ELENA
(turning a page)
From whom.
MARCUS
You know from whom.

ELENA closes the book. She does not look at him.

ELENA
What did it say.
MARCUS
Thatshe'swell.Thatshe'scomingbackinthespring.Thatshewould
like to see us. Both of us.

= Elena considers throwing the book.

ELENA
"Both of us."
MARCUS
That's what it said.

Thelampgoesoutcompletely.Neitherofthemmoves.AfteramomentELENAstrikesamatch.Thelightcomesback,smallerthanbefore.

# SCENE 2

Thelamphasgoneoutagain,properlythistime.ELENAisalone,standingatthewindow.Thewindhasstopped.Thesilence isworse.

ELENA
(to the dark)
I knew you would.

She does not turn when MARCUS enters quietly behind her.

MARCUS
Knew I would what.
ELENA
Write back.

A beat.

MARCUS
I haven't yet.
ELENA
But you will.

He doesn't answer. She finally turns.

.ELENA

I'm not asking you to choose.
MARCUS
I know.
ELENA
I'm telling you that you already have.

Lights fade.

# ACT TWO

= Same room. The thaw, and what it brings up out of theground.

# SCENE 1

= Test

The same room, mid-morning. Sunlight where there hasbeennonefor three days
.ELENApoursteaforone. Thelampisstillonthetable
,unlit,spotless.ThereisnosignofMARCUS.

She lifts the cup. She does not drink.

ELENA
(softly)
Alright.

A KNOCK at the door. She does not move.

ELENA
(to herself)
Alright.

Anotherknock.Shesetsthecupdownwithoutspillingitandcrossestothedoor.Shedoesnotopenit.

ELENA
(through the door)
Tell her the road's open now.

She returns to the table and sits in MARCUS's chair.

End of play.

